{
 "bead": "wb-km7q.5",
 "requirement": "SDK-REACTIVE-FIBER-ADAPTIVE-COMPUTATION-AND-CONTROL-R14",
 "measured": "read-only git show, git grep -n -w, git ls-tree and git rev-parse on the local ReactiveFiberTSXSDK clone (origin/main at its last fetch) and the installed rf, by seat ws-03 of run g10-work-s125, 2026-10-28",
 "producer": {
  "repo": "ReactiveFiberTSXSDK",
  "doc": "docs/programs/reactive-fiber-adaptive-computation-and-control-2026-10-17.md",
  "lines": {
   "3": {
    "text": "**Date:** 2026-10-17. **Status:** proposed extensions; none of the new exports claimed shipped. **Branch:** main. **Canonical program:** [Adaptive Computation and Control](https://github.com/jehalladay/FiberOpticsResearch/tree/main/docs/research/foa/programs/adaptive-computation-and-control-2026-10-17). **Work packages:** AC-01, AC-04, AC-10, AC-15.",
    "sha256": "ec7457829e2137aefb8e88f4451d1155db1d93bf002cd58d6de8b2c1cefef58b"
   },
   "11": {
    "text": "**Hooks:** `useSignal`, `useDerivedSignal`, `useWindow`, `useEWMA`, `useHysteresis`, `useDerivative`, `useFreshness`, `useDemand`, `useSpeculation`, `useResourcePressure`, `useController`, `useEvidence`, `useContextUtility` and `useTrace`. Prefer hook wrappers over Fiber-optic operators; do not implement competing temporal operator engines per TSX component.",
    "sha256": "6a2321db8f02a0919398d6d140d6c7e7c9234736bbf4fd9e35b8f966d2ae00fb"
   },
   "13": {
    "text": "**Boundaries:** `ResourceBoundary` (freshness/stale-while-refresh), `SpeculationBoundary` (scoped budget and admission), `ControlBoundary` (temporal controller/actuator scope), `SnapshotBoundary` (coherent or explicitly bounded-stale dependency), `EffectBoundary` (extension of existing effect/commit scope). An 'InferenceBoundary' and 'CacheBoundary' are convenience compositions unless the owner demonstrates an irreducible new semantic need.",
    "sha256": "b0c78979414ca9af741d06b2eccba6e69aed3956d4513a30637af41e5085b9c4"
   },
   "17": {
    "text": "Every new hook consumes one stable dispatcher slot each render and returns a read-only view plus optional callback handle. It may read the frozen snapshot and append a **declaration** to the render attempt. It must never directly poll, launch a model call, revise global admission, mutate controller state or perform I/O while rendering. On suspension, error, aborted attempt or replaced render, interest/controller/effect declarations are discarded just as existing effects are. After host commit, the broker can admit work and publish a new resource version, waking dependent components.",
    "sha256": "6f00524d63b0e8db4413d6393acbae9cec3dbb6578589230abcf1ae875fbe644"
   },
   "19": {
    "text": "`useSpeculation` must be dynamically adjustable via component props/hooks and via event/host callback methods `revise`, `withdraw`, `promote`. These callback methods are invalid in render; promotion declares actual demand but does not guarantee scheduling or reuse. Component unmount withdraws only its interest, not another consumer's shared execution.",
    "sha256": "086da26348a10d28f41714e9b83fd0fa62c2eeef2f50f7e8b1338de39f2baf01"
   },
   "48": {
    "text": "T0 API/ADR conflict inventory and current golden export capability audit.",
    "sha256": "fa976ecf85c74629d931e41bdd05c5fd0934778cd7e3ef5b9250e48cabef14b1"
   },
   "49": {
    "text": "T1 pure hook slots/conditional hook failure and suspension/effect rollback.",
    "sha256": "54b2e7cce4ff5d3562024dc5cf1f4606afb3e7fda8c1a0d21878900274fb3db1"
   },
   "50": {
    "text": "T2 resource boundary with stale+pending, null-ready and failed data.",
    "sha256": "48e28f309a8b1b63725f0cd754671b2e366a5ca4f31e094d0bd8e7694625da17"
   },
   "51": {
    "text": "T3 speculative intent creation/revision/withdrawal and shared execution (fake host).",
    "sha256": "b84fac3a93b4c061e049f52ddeb61a06ccb9d07431ff6454c0258089c48db24d"
   },
   "52": {
    "text": "T4 real Fiber/Lens/inference host promotion, generation check and no duplicate effect dispatch.",
    "sha256": "1914f8d23539d362fa6b611e85ce7e951ebcf9201bccd7a5ac40133443ea7393"
   },
   "53": {
    "text": "T5 controller temporal state and single applied actuator integration.",
    "sha256": "c2fc8ea7a209a6dcbc2d405a721d290ce08d3ebc9596f89c302a686b47996dd4"
   },
   "54": {
    "text": "T6 Forge local gates, installed npm/bridge consumer and current performance benchmark parity. No 'green' claim from old pinned plans or tests alone.",
    "sha256": "68c2cdb84946a11cf0c889286b3c67a69353c0639592c81b4c3bb8ff55c0c71a"
   },
   "58": {
    "text": "No second Fiber scheduler, no TSX runtime authority over host clocks, no unconditional model speculation, no giant new UX DSL, no dependency on DevTools or Mechanical/MicroPolicyCLI packages. Publish new exports only when implementation and installed tests exist.",
    "sha256": "2e4ae1c349d1ea95e464c778d6789d72eeb58f484a295e695764ec41eeb7098a"
   }
  },
